  "root_problem": "Dispute tickets doubled from a ~600/month baseline to 1180 (Aug) and 1260 (Sep) 2026 (E-07). For the ESTIMATED-read subset of disputed bills (1240 of 3025, E-02), the dominant cause is a billing-import rejection: 1184 of these had an AMI read received before cutoff but were rejected as REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION, forcing estimate substitution (E-11), coincident with validation rule BV-17 (deployed 2026-08-01) comparing raw register values to 12-month m3 history with no unit scaling (E-12), applied to AMI firmware v4.2 (rollout 2026-06) whose register output is in 0.1 m3 units versus legacy v3.x's whole-m3 units (E-13) — a mismatch that would make normal consumption appear tenfold inflated and be falsely flagged as high-consumption by BV-17. This mechanism explains only the ESTIMATED-read dispute subset; the majority of disputes occur on ACTUAL-read bills (1785 of 3025, E-02) and their cause is not yet identified by current evidence."
 },
